{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27442": {
      "title": "Workforce and Organizational Development Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor (Non-Tenured,F0586A)",
      "description": "ODU - Job Site | Workforce and Organizational Development Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor (Non-Tenured,F0586A) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Interest Cards/Categories Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ Applicant Alternative Hiring FAQ Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty Applicants: Contact Human Resources at: (757) 683-3042 HRRecruitment@odu.edu Teaching and Research Faculty Applicants: Contact Academic Affairs at: aafacultyemployment@odu.edu Workforce and Organizational Development Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor (Non-Tenured,F0586A) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates must apply via https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27399 and attach the following: A cover letter detailing relevant experience with the required and preferred qualifications outlined in this job posting. A curriculum vitae. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Contact information for three professional references. When your application is submitted, the application site will request letters of recommendation from these individuals. Review of applications will begin February 15, 2027, and continue until the position is filled. For questions and inquiries, please contact Dr. Michelle Bartlett, Search Committee Chair, at mbartlet@odu.edu. Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Workforce and Organizational Development Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor (Non-Tenured,F0586A) Department ED FOUNDATIONS & LEADERSHIP Position Number F0586A Job Description Old Dominion University’s Department of Educational Leadership & Workforce Development seeks applications for a full-time Assistant/Associate Professor (10-month appointment with summer employment) in the Workforce & Organizational Development (graduate) program beginning July 2027. Candidates with expertise in human resource development and training, workforce development, and career and technical education are encouraged to apply. The salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. A Ph.D. or Ed.D. is required in a field related to human resource development-training, workforce and organizational development, career and technical education, or equivalent that will enable the candidate to teach graduate courses, advise MS students, and serve on dissertation committees. Responsibilities include: Teaching and developing graduate level online courses, Advising and directing graduate student coursework, Mentoring graduate student research, and Support administrative functions of the MS Workforce and Talent Development program. Previous college teaching and/or business and industry experience in the following fields is preferred: career and technical education, business and industry training/adult education; organizational and workforce development; organizational performance improvement; program evaluation and assessment; project management; consulting; and learning analytics. Position Type FullTime Type of Recruitment General Public Type of Recruitment General Public Minimum required education and/or special licenses, registrations, trainings, or certifications A Ph.D. or Ed.D. is required in a field related to Human Resource Development-Training, Career and Technical Education, Workforce & Organizational Development, or an equivalent that will enable the candidate to specialize in an area of research, teaching, and service. Minimum required level and type of experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities Proven ability to teach online courses effectively. Experience mentoring graduate students. Demonstrated ability to lead academic programs. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively in a diverse academic community. Preferred Qualifications Experience in delivering online courses in different modalities is preferred, e.g., synchronous, asynchronous, and blended. The candidate is expected to demonstrate a commitment to diversity and inclusiveness and a willingness to work in a multicultural setting, as well as a commitment to participating in program governance and decision-making. Experience with program development or curriculum design. Scholarly writing experience, including publishing peer reviewed manuscripts. A background overlapping more than one of career and technical education, human resources training, workforce development, and the community college system. Conditions of Employment Location Norfolk, VA Job Open Date 11/02/2026 Application Review Date 02/15/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Application Instructions Interested candidates must apply via https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27399 and attach the following: A cover letter detailing relevant experience with the required and preferred qualifications outlined in this job posting. A curriculum vitae. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Contact information for three professional references. When your application is submitted, the application site will request letters of recommendation from these individuals. Review of applications will begin February 15, 2027, and continue until the position is filled. For questions and inquiries, please contact Dr. Michelle Bartlett, Search Committee Chair, at mbartlet@odu.edu. Telework Friendly No Reasonable Accommodation Request If you are an individual with a disability and require reasonable accommodation, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757)683-3141. Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or © consistent with contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. About the College https://www.odu.edu/education About the Department The Department of Educational Leadership & Workforce Development is one of five departments in the Darden College of Education and Professional Studies. The department has twenty full-time faculty that offer graduate programs in Workforce and Organizational Development, Community College Leadership, Educational Leadership, and Higher Education Leadership. The department offers an undergraduate degree in Occupational & Technical Studies with majors in Fashion Merchandising, Industrial Technology, Training Specialist, as well as a degree in Career & Technical Education with majors in Marketing Education and Technology Education. For more information, visit: https://www.odu.edu/educational-foundations-leadership Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education (website or print) Higheredjobs.com DiverseJobs.com InsightIntoDiversity.com Jobs.Virginia.gov Old Dominion University website Virginia Pilot (website or print) Richmond Times Dispatch (website or print) Academic Keys Other If you selected \"Other,\" how did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Contact Information for Professional References Optional Documents If you have questions: Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty applicants, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757) 683-3042 or Jobsearch@odu.edu . Teaching and Research Faculty applicants, please contact the Office of Academic Affairs at aafacultyemployment@odu.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27374": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professors (2) of Library &amp; Information Sciences (Non-Tenure Track)",
      "description": "ODU - Job Site | Teaching Assistant Professors (2) of Library &amp; Information Sciences (Non-Tenure Track) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Interest Cards/Categories Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ Applicant Alternative Hiring FAQ Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty Applicants: Contact Human Resources at: (757) 683-3042 HRRecruitment@odu.edu Teaching and Research Faculty Applicants: Contact Academic Affairs at: aafacultyemployment@odu.edu Teaching Assistant Professors (2) of Library & Information Sciences (Non-Tenure Track) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates must submit application materials to https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27361 including the following: Letter of Interest. Curriculum Vitae. Statement of Teaching Philosophy. Unofficial Graduate Transcripts. Names and contact information for three professional references. For questions concerning the position, please contact the chair of the search committee, Dr. Elizabeth Burns, eburns@odu.edu . Review of applications will begin on November 23, 2026, and the position will remain open until it is filled. Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Teaching Assistant Professors (2) of Library & Information Sciences (Non-Tenure Track) Department STEM ED/PROF STUDIES Position Number F1097A F0970A Job Description The Department of STEM Education & Professional Studies seeks applicants for a 10-month faculty position as a Lecturer of Library & Information Studies to start July 25, 2027 . The primary responsibilities for this position are: To develop and teach graduate, distance learning courses in library and information studies. To participate in the administration and recruitment initiatives of the Master of Library and Information Studies program. To develop and maintain relationships with employers in libraries, archives, and other related institutions to assist with recruitment, program growth, and placements. To participate in the professional and intellectual community through service in the program, department, and college. The Department of STEM Education and Professional Studies is proud to support a diverse and inclusive culture. Individuals from underrepresented populations are encouraged to apply. Position Type FullTime Type of Recruitment General Public Type of Recruitment General Public Minimum required education and/or special licenses, registrations, trainings, or certifications The minimum requirement for this position is a Master of Library Science or equivalent degree from a program accredited by the American Library Association. Minimum required level and type of experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities ALA Accredited MLIS Experience teaching online courses. Evidence of teaching ability in library, information, archival and/or technology studies. Professional experience in academic, public, school, or special libraries or other information fields. Excellence in written and oral communication. Preferred Qualifications ● Doctoral degree in Library and Information studies or related area of study, ● Experience teaching in an online, asynchronous environment, ● Experience teaching online, graduate-level courses, ● Experience with course development ● Expertise and experience in the areas of digital scholarship, archival studies, special collections (rare books and manuscripts), and scholarly communications, or school librarianship ● Demonstrated breadth of knowledge of the library profession ● Evidence of a commitment to student success. Conditions of Employment N/A Location Norfolk, VA Job Open Date 10/12/2026 Application Review Date 11/23/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Application Instructions Interested candidates must submit application materials to https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27361 including the following: Letter of Interest. Curriculum Vitae. Statement of Teaching Philosophy. Unofficial Graduate Transcripts. Names and contact information for three professional references. For questions concerning the position, please contact the chair of the search committee, Dr. Elizabeth Burns, eburns@odu.edu . Review of applications will begin on November 23, 2026, and the position will remain open until it is filled. Telework Friendly Yes Reasonable Accommodation Request If you are an individual with a disability and require reasonable accommodation, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757)683-3141. Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or © consistent with contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. About the College https://www.odu.edu/eps About the Department https://www.odu.edu/stemps Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education (website or print) Higheredjobs.com DiverseJobs.com InsightIntoDiversity.com Jobs.Virginia.gov Old Dominion University website Virginia Pilot (website or print) Richmond Times Dispatch (website or print) Academic Keys Other If you selected \"Other,\" how did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Contact Information for Professional References Optional Documents If you have questions: Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty applicants, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757) 683-3042 or Jobsearch@odu.edu . Teaching and Research Faculty applicants, please contact the Office of Academic Affairs at aafacultyemployment@odu.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
