    "https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27292": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor &amp; Inaugural Chair of the Department of Health Behavior, Policy &amp; Management (Tenured Track F0129A)",
      "description": "ODU - Job Site | Associate or Full Professor &amp; Inaugural Chair of the Department of Health Behavior, Policy &amp; Management (Tenured Track F0129A) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Interest Cards/Categories Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ Applicant Alternative Hiring FAQ Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty Applicants: Contact Human Resources at: (757) 683-3042 HRRecruitment@odu.edu Teaching and Research Faculty Applicants: Contact Academic Affairs at: aafacultyemployment@odu.edu Associate or Full Professor & Inaugural Chair of the Department of Health Behavior, Policy & Management (Tenured Track F0129A) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must apply at https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27270 and submit each of the following required documents: Cover letter concisely addressing the required and preferred qualification bullets listed above. Current curriculum vita. Concise vision statement for department development. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Contact information for three (3) professional references. Applications must be submitted by November 30, 2026 for full consideration. The position will remain open until it is filled. Questions about the position should be directed to the search committee Chair, Dr. Poplin, at gpoplin@odu.edu . Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Associate or Full Professor & Inaugural Chair of the Department of Health Behavior, Policy & Management (Tenured Track F0129A) Department MASTERS IN PUBLIC HEALTH Position Number F0129A Job Description The Joint School of Public Health ( JSPH ) at Old Dominion University ( ODU ) and Norfolk State University ( NSU ) in Norfolk, Virginia invites applications from experienced, accomplished, and visionary individuals to serve as inaugural Chair of the Department of Health Behavior, Policy, & Management ( HBPM ). The Chair is expected to provide visionary leadership in departmental education, research, and service activities in alignment with the School and University’s strategic plan. The Council on Education for Public Health ( CEPH ) formally acted to accredit JSPH in June 2026. The programs within JSPH accredited by CEPH include the Bachelor of Science in Environmental Health ( BSEH ), Bachelor of Science in Public Health ( BSPH ), Master of Public Health ( MPH ), and Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in Health Services Research. The Master of Healthcare Administration ( MHA ) program is housed within JSPH but is not governed under CEPH accreditation. The HBPM Department benefits from a distinguished faculty with extensive expertise in health behavior, policy, and management. Our professors are recognized leaders in their fields, combining rigorous academic training with practical experience in public health practice. They bring a wealth of knowledge from diverse backgrounds, including social and behavioral sciences, policy analysis, and health administration, ensuring a comprehensive and forward-thinking educational experience. Their commitment to mentoring, research, and community engagement enriches the learning environment, preparing students to address complex health challenges with innovative solutions and effective management strategies. The JSPH has selected WittKieffer, a premier executive search and advisory solutions firm, to assist with this recruitment. Candidate inquiries, nominations or requests for additional information can be sent through the office of Cody Burke, via email, at cburke@wittkieffer.com Position Type FullTime Type of Recruitment General Public Type of Recruitment General Public Minimum required education and/or special licenses, registrations, trainings, or certifications Applicants must hold an earned terminal doctoral degree (Ph.D., Dr.P.H., or Sc.D.) in Health Behavior, Health Promotion, Health Education, Health Policy, Health Management or Administration, Health Services Research, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Alternatively, candidates may have earned an M.D. degree from an accredited program with a graduate degree in public health (M.P.H. or equivalent) from an accredited public health program or school. Minimum required level and type of experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities A sustained record of peer-reviewed scholarship in health behavior, health promotion, health policy, health management, health services research, or a closely related area, sufficient to qualify for appointment with tenure at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor at ODU . A minimum of five (5) years of full-time faculty experience at the rank of Assistant Professor or above at an accredited institution of higher education. Demonstrated success in securing external research, training, or programmatic funding as Principal Investigator, Multiple Principal Investigator, or Project/Core Lead, including at least one competitively awarded, investigator-initiated or unsolicited award. Formal academic administrative experience; for example, as department chair or vice chair, division head, graduate or academic program director, center or institute director, or an equivalent unit-level leadership role that included direct responsibility for personnel decisions and budget planning or management. Experience teaching and mentoring students at the graduate level, including thesis, dissertation, or capstone supervision. Experience in faculty mentoring, workload assignment, and performance evaluation, including participation in annual review or promotion and tenure processes. Demonstrated ability to build and sustain collaborative working relationships across academic units, institutions, and/or community and practice partners. Excellent interpersonal skills and oral and written communication skills. Eligibility for appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor with tenure at ODU , consistent with the ODU Faculty Handbook ( https://itsapps.odu.edu/ao/facultyhandbook/index.php?page=ch02s24.html ). Preferred Qualifications Prior service as a department chair, vice chair, division head, or equivalent academic unit leader at a research-intensive institution. Direct, hands-on experience with CEPH accreditation, e.g., self-study preparation, criterion response, competency mapping, or site visit management. Experience leading an academic unit through significant organizational change, such as the formation of a new department or school, an institutional merger or consolidation, or a multi-campus or multi-institution partnership. A demonstrated record of growing sponsored research activity within a unit, mentoring faculty to independent funding, assembling interdisciplinary teams, or building center-scale or training-grant programs. Scholarly or professional expertise spanning at least one of the department’s core areas: health behavior, health promotion, health policy, health management and administration, and health services research. A clear, forward-thinking vision for advancing the reputation, research profile, and visibility of the Department, School, and University. A record of community-engaged scholarship or practice, including sustained partnership with state or local health departments, health systems, or community-based organizations. Experience collaborating with an academic health center or health system, relevant to the Department’s opportunities within Macon and Joan Brock Virginia Health Sciences at ODU . Experience with program and curriculum development, revision, and assessment at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, including online or on-campus delivery. A demonstrated record of success in student recruitment, retention, and career placement. Experience mentoring doctoral students and chairing dissertation committees. National professional visibility, such as service on federal study sections or review panels, editorial boards, or in leadership roles within professional associations (e.g., APHA , AcademyHealth, AUPHA , ASPPH , SOPHE , or ACHE ). Familiarity with the health and workforce needs of coastal, rural, and military-connected communities, and with the public health landscape of the Hampton Roads region. Conditions of Employment Location Norfolk, VA Job Open Date 09/21/2026 Application Review Date 11/30/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Application Instructions Applicants must apply at https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27270 and submit each of the following required documents: Cover letter concisely addressing the required and preferred qualification bullets listed above. Current curriculum vita. Concise vision statement for department development. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Contact information for three (3) professional references. Applications must be submitted by November 30, 2026 for full consideration. The position will remain open until it is filled. Questions about the position should be directed to the search committee Chair, Dr. Poplin, at gpoplin@odu.edu . Telework Friendly No Reasonable Accommodation Request If you are an individual with a disability and require reasonable accommodation, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757)683-3141. Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or © consistent with contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. About the College The Joint School of Public Health is a partnership between Old Dominion University and Norfolk State University. Its expertise and collaboration embody forward-thinking and community-responsive approaches to public health education and outreach located at both campuses. Information regarding public health at ODU and NSU , visit https://www.odu.edu/public-health and https://www.nsu.edu/public-health . For information about the recent integration of Eastern Virginia Medical School into Old Dominion University to create the Macon and Joan Brock Virginia Health Sciences at Old Dominion University, please visit https://www.odu.edu/article/macon-joan-brock-virginia-health-sciences-at-old-dominion-university-launches . About the Department The Department of Health Behavior, Policy and Management ( HBPM ) is dedicated to shaping future leaders in health behavior, policy, management, and research. We tackle critical population and organizational challenges through a blend of innovative education, cutting-edge research, and practical application. Our health behavior experts are committed to advancing public health by addressing the root causes of health issues. Meanwhile, our health policy and management specialists focus on creating evidence-based solutions to systemic challenges, preparing the next generation of healthcare administrators, policymakers, and researchers to ensure accessible, high-quality care for all. Learn more about the HBPM Department at: https://www.odu.edu/health-behavior-policy-management . Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education (website or print) Higheredjobs.com DiverseJobs.com InsightIntoDiversity.com Jobs.Virginia.gov Old Dominion University website Virginia Pilot (website or print) Richmond Times Dispatch (website or print) Academic Keys Other If you selected \"Other,\" how did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Other Document Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Contact Information for Professional References Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests If you have questions: Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty applicants, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757) 683-3042 or Jobsearch@odu.edu . Teaching and Research Faculty applicants, please contact the Office of Academic Affairs at aafacultyemployment@odu.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27272": {
      "title": "Associate Director Community Psychological Services Clinic, Clinical Professor (Non-Tenured Track, F0465A)",
      "description": "ODU - Job Site | Associate Director Community Psychological Services Clinic, Clinical Professor (Non-Tenured Track, F0465A) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Interest Cards/Categories Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ Applicant Alternative Hiring FAQ Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty Applicants: Contact Human Resources at: (757) 683-3042 HRRecruitment@odu.edu Teaching and Research Faculty Applicants: Contact Academic Affairs at: aafacultyemployment@odu.edu Associate Director Community Psychological Services Clinic, Clinical Professor (Non-Tenured Track, F0465A) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates must apply at https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/26605 and attach the following with their online application: : · Cover letter of application summarizing their relevant qualifications for the position including prior relevant experience and clinical theoretical orientation Full curriculum vitae Statement of philosophy and prior experience in providing clinical supervision. Unofficial Transcripts Full contact information for at least three academic or professional references. Applications will be reviewed as they are received and will continue until the position is filled, with priority given to applications received by August 17, 2026 . Inquiries regarding this position may be directed to Dr. Christina Rodriguez, Search Committee Chair, via email at crodriguez@odu.edu. Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Associate Director Community Psychological Services Clinic, Clinical Professor (Non-Tenured Track, F0465A) Department PSYCHOLOGY DEPARTMENT Position Number F0465A Job Description The Department of Psychology at Old Dominion University ( ODU ) seeks to fill a full-time 12-month non-tenure track faculty position to serve as the Associate Director of the Community Psychological Services Center ( CPSC ), beginning January 2027 . The Associate Director of the Center will be an integral member of the ODU Clinical Psychology PhD Program faculty and serve as Associate Director of Clinical Training for the Program. The CPSC is a new outpatient facility adjacent to ODU campus that will provide mental health assessment and therapeutic services to the Hampton Roads community. The CPSC is prepared to provide individual and group psychotherapy for adults, children and youth, and families as well as psychodiagnostics assessments. The facility will also serve as a core clinical training and research site for students in ODU’s Clinical Psychology PhD Program, who will provide direct clinical services. Primary responsibilities will include: Primary and secondary supervision of graduate students using evidence-based and culturally responsive assessment and treatment for diverse populations; Meeting with appropriate university administrators, private referral sources, public and community agencies, and organizations interested in CPSC programs and services; Cultivating external practicum sites in the Hampton Roads community; Direct provision of mental health services. Conforming to the professional standards and ethics of the American Psychological Association and any other accrediting bodies and adhere with state and federal laws regarding the delivery of mental health services. Position Type FullTime Type of Recruitment General Public Type of Recruitment General Public Minimum required education and/or special licenses, registrations, trainings, or certifications Candidates must have a doctoral degree in clinical psychology or closely related field from an APA -accredited program and APA -accredited internship or its equivalent; Licensure or licensure-eligible in the Commonwealth of Virginia prior to the start date Minimum required level and type of experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities Applicants must have a record of at least one year of providing clinical supervision; At least one year of experience post-doctoral in provision of health service psychology services. Preferred Qualifications Expertise in psychodiagnostic assessment; Expertise in delivery of mental health services to children and families. Proficiency in a range of treatment modalities (e.g., CBT approaches, third-wave behavioral therapy; family/systems approaches, trauma-focused approaches, etc.) Conditions of Employment This is a site based position requiring in person work. Location Norfolk, VA Job Open Date 12/25/2026 Application Review Date 08/17/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Application Instructions Interested candidates must apply at https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/26605 and attach the following with their online application: : · Cover letter of application summarizing their relevant qualifications for the position including prior relevant experience and clinical theoretical orientation Full curriculum vitae Statement of philosophy and prior experience in providing clinical supervision. Unofficial Transcripts Full contact information for at least three academic or professional references. Applications will be reviewed as they are received and will continue until the position is filled, with priority given to applications received by August 17, 2026 . Inquiries regarding this position may be directed to Dr. Christina Rodriguez, Search Committee Chair, via email at crodriguez@odu.edu. Telework Friendly No Reasonable Accommodation Request If you are an individual with a disability and require reasonable accommodation, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757)683-3141. Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or © consistent with contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. About the College Old Dominion University, located in Norfolk, is Virginia’s forward-focused public doctoral research university with more than 23,000 students, an R1 research ranking, rigorous academics, an energetic residential community and initiatives that contribute $2.6 billion annually to Virginia’s economy. About the Department The Department of Psychology is one of seven departments in the College of Sciences and includes 29 full-time faculty members, over 1,200 undergraduate majors, and 60 students in our graduate programs. The department offers a terminal Master’s degree in Psychology and a Ph.D. with concentrations in Health Psychology, Human Factors, and Clinical Psychology. For more information about the department, visit https://www.odu.edu/psychology . Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education (website or print) Higheredjobs.com DiverseJobs.com InsightIntoDiversity.com Jobs.Virginia.gov Old Dominion University website Virginia Pilot (website or print) Richmond Times Dispatch (website or print) Academic Keys Other If you selected \"Other,\" how did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently employed by, or have previously been employed by, Old Dominion University or Eastern Virginia Medical Center? Yes No If yes, provide dates of employment. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Other Document Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Contact Information for Professional References Optional Documents If you have questions: Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty applicants, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757) 683-3042 or Jobsearch@odu.edu . Teaching and Research Faculty applicants, please contact the Office of Academic Affairs at aafacultyemployment@odu.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
