ching responsibilities will include both undergraduate and graduate-level courses. The candidate is expected to teach tax and other areas of accounting. Apply by October 15, 2026 for full consideration. The position will remain open until filled. Position Type FullTime Type of Recruitment General Public Type of Recruitment General Public Minimum required education and/or special licenses, registrations, trainings, or certifications A Ph.D. in Accounting or related field from an AACSB -accredited institution by the time of appointment Minimum required level and type of experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities Eligible to meet ODU criteria for Scholarly Academic status Demonstrated teaching experience in accounting Preferred Qualifications Record of scholarly activity, including publications in high-quality, peer-reviewed journals. Teaching experience and interest in taxation and/or across multiple areas of accounting. Relevant professional or industry experience in taxation Professional certification (i.e., CPA , CMA , etc.) Conditions of Employment Location Norfolk, VA Job Open Date 07/07/2026 Application Review Date 10/15/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Application Instructions Interested candidates should apply electronically at https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/26761 and submit: Letter of application indicating qualifications and interest. Current Curriculum Vitae. Transcripts Contact information of three references. For additional information, contact Dr. Hong Kim Duong, chair of the search committee at 757-683-4025 or via e-mail at hkduong@odu.edu. Telework Friendly No Reasonable Accommodation Request If you are an individual with a disability and require reasonable accommodation, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757)683-3141. Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or © consistent with contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. About the College The Strome College of Business offers undergraduate programs, masters degrees in accounting, economics, and public administration, an MBA , a PhD with concentrations in finance, marketing, management, and information technology, and PhD programs in business and public administration and urban policy. The College is fully AACSB accredited with separate AACSB accreditation for the accounting programs. About the Department The School of Accountancy offers a Master of Science in Accounting and BSBA in Accounting, in face-to-face and online teaching environments. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education (website or print) Higheredjobs.com DiverseJobs.com InsightIntoDiversity.com Jobs.Virginia.gov Old Dominion University website Virginia Pilot (website or print) Richmond Times Dispatch (website or print) Academic Keys Other * If you selected \"Other,\" how did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently employed by, or have previously been employed by, Old Dominion University or Eastern Virginia Medical Center? Yes No * If yes, provide dates of employment. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Con