      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in Philosophy and Religious Studies",
      "description": "ODU - Job Site | Adjunct Faculty in Philosophy and Religious Studies Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Interest Cards/Categories Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ Applicant Alternative Hiring FAQ Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty Applicants: Contact Human Resources at: (757) 683-3042 HRRecruitment@odu.edu Teaching and Research Faculty Applicants: Contact Academic Affairs at: aafacultyemployment@odu.edu Adjunct Faculty in Philosophy and Religious Studies Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested Candidates must apply via https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/26117 And submit: A short cover letter outlining preparation for and/or experience in teaching courses in Philosophy and/or Religious Studies; A Curriculum Vitae; Unofficial graduate transcripts. and Contact information for 3 professional references. Review of applications will begin August 15, 2026, and will recur whenever openings arise. Only those selected for interviews will be contacted. Questions or requests for additional information can be directed to Dr. Nicole Willock, Chair of Philosophy and Religious Studies, via email at nwillock@odu.edu Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Adjunct Faculty in Philosophy and Religious Studies Department PHILOSOPHY Position Number PT0230 Job Description The Department of Philosophy & Religious Studies invites applicants for part-time adjunct instructional faculty to teach courses within the fields of Philosophy or Religious Studies. We have the most need for in-person classes on the Norfolk campus for general education courses taught within the department as well as 8-week online asynchronous classes in courses, such as Bioethics, Cybersecurity Ethics, Business Ethics, and popular general education courses, such as REL 147: Cults and Conspiracies. This post will remain open for applications as opportunities arise throughout the 2026-27 academic year, and beyond. Position Type Part-Time Type of Recruitment General Public Type of Recruitment General Public Minimum required education and/or special licenses, registrations, trainings, or certifications M.A. or Ph.D. in Philosophy or Religious Studies or an M.A. or Ph.D. in a related field with a minimum of 18 hours graduate credits in Philosophy or Religious Studies courses. Minimum required level and type of experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities Excellent written and oral communication skills Experience with online teaching in higher education, especially use of Canvas. Preparation for and/or experience in teaching Philosophy or Religious Studies courses at the college level. Preferred Qualifications Conditions of Employment Location Norfolk, VA Job Open Date 07/25/2026 Application Review Date Open Until Filled Yes Application Instructions Interested Candidates must apply via https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/26117 And submit: A short cover letter outlining preparation for and/or experience in teaching courses in Philosophy and/or Religious Studies; A Curriculum Vitae; Unofficial graduate transcripts. and Contact information for 3 professional references. Review of applications will begin August 15, 2026, and will recur whenever openings arise. Only those selected for interviews will be contacted. Questions or requests for additional information can be directed to Dr. Nicole Willock, Chair of Philosophy and Religious Studies, via email at nwillock@odu.edu Telework Friendly No Reasonable Accommodation Request If you are an individual with a disability and require reasonable accommodation, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757)683-3141. Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or © consistent with contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. About the College https://www.odu.edu/arts-letters About the Department https://www.odu.edu/philosophy Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education (website or print) Higheredjobs.com DiverseJobs.com InsightIntoDiversity.com Jobs.Virginia.gov Old Dominion University website Virginia Pilot (website or print) Richmond Times Dispatch (website or print) Academic Keys Other If you selected \"Other,\" how did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently employed by, or have previously been employed by, Old Dominion University or Eastern Virginia Medical Center? Yes No If yes, provide dates of employment. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Contact Information for Professional References Optional Documents If you have questions: Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty applicants, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757) 683-3042 or Jobsearch@odu.edu . Teaching and Research Faculty applicants, please contact the Office of Academic Affairs at aafacultyemployment@odu.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
