    "https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/26838": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in Sociology and Criminal Justice",
      "description": "ODU - Job Site | Adjunct Faculty in Sociology and Criminal Justice Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Interest Cards/Categories Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ Applicant Alternative Hiring FAQ Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty Applicants: Contact Human Resources at: (757) 683-3042 HRRecruitment@odu.edu Teaching and Research Faculty Applicants: Contact Academic Affairs at: aafacultyemployment@odu.edu Adjunct Faculty in Sociology and Criminal Justice Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates must apply via; https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/25477 and submit the following: A cover letter detailing preparation and experience teaching in the fields of Criminal Justice, Criminology, Cynercriminology, and/or Sociology. A curriculum vita. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Contact information for three professional references. Application review will recur whenever openings arise. Only those selected for interviews will be contacted. Questions or requests for additional information can be sent to Dr. Ruth Triplett, chair of the search committee, via email at rtriplet@odu.edu. Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Adjunct Faculty in Sociology and Criminal Justice Department SOCIOLOGY Position Number PT0270 Job Description The Department of Sociology and Criminal Justice at Old Dominion University invites applicants for part-time Adjunct instructional positions. Adjunct instructional faculty mostly teach 200-level sections of in-person Introduction to Sociology and Introduction to Criminology courses, with an opportunity to teach upper-level electives in Sociology, Criminal Justice, and Cybercriminology, depending on department needs and applicant qualifications. We tend to have the greatest need for instructors who can teach between 8:00 am and 3:00 pm. Position Type Part-Time Type of Recruitment General Public Type of Recruitment General Public Minimum required education and/or special licenses, registrations, trainings, or certifications M.S, M.A, or Ph.D. in Sociology, Criminal Justice, Criminology or closely related fields with a minimum of 18 hours graduate credit hours in Sociology. Criminal Justice or Criminology. JD is required for those teaching law-related classes. Minimum required level and type of experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities Preferred Qualifications Availability to teach in-person on Old Dominon University’s Norfolk, VA campus between the hours of 8:00 AM and 3:00 pm. Conditions of Employment Location Norfolk, VA Job Open Date 08/03/2026 Application Review Date Open Until Filled Yes Application Instructions Interested candidates must apply via; https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/25477 and submit the following: A cover letter detailing preparation and experience teaching in the fields of Criminal Justice, Criminology, Cynercriminology, and/or Sociology. A curriculum vita. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Contact information for three professional references. Application review will recur whenever openings arise. Only those selected for interviews will be contacted. Questions or requests for additional information can be sent to Dr. Ruth Triplett, chair of the search committee, via email at rtriplet@odu.edu. Telework Friendly No Reasonable Accommodation Request If you are an individual with a disability and require reasonable accommodation, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757)683-3141. Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision 