    "https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/25605": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in English",
      "description": "ODU - Job Site | Adjunct Faculty in English Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Interest Cards/Categories Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ Applicant Alternative Hiring FAQ Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty Applicants: Contact Human Resources at: (757) 683-3042 HRRecruitment@odu.edu Teaching and Research Faculty Applicants: Contact Academic Affairs at: aafacultyemployment@odu.edu Adjunct Faculty in English Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates must apply via https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/21039 and submit a cover letter outlining preparation and experience for teaching General Education Composition and/or Literature courses; a curriculum vitae; unofficial graduate transcripts; and contact information for 3 professional references. Applications will begin July 22, 2025, and and will recur whenever openings arise. Only those selected for interviews will be contacted. Questions or requests for additional information can be sent to Dr. Mary Beth Pennington, chair of the search committee, via e-mail at mpenning@odu.edu . Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Adjunct Faculty in English Department ENGLISH Position Number PT0110 Job Description The English Department at Old Dominion University invites applicants for part-time Adjunct instructional faculty teach 100- and 200- level sections of in-person General Education Composition and Literature courses. We are currently seeking individuals , this post may remain open for additional applications as opportunities arise. Those selected will be hired as part of an adjunct pool, which will be utilized as needed based on which courses are in need of coverage. We tend to have the greatest need for instructors who can teach daytime, on-campus courses between 8:00 AM and 3:00 PM, most often in General Education Composition but sometimes also in General Education Literature. Position Type Part-Time Type of Recruitment General Public Type of Recruitment General Public Minimum required education and/or special licenses, registrations, trainings, or certifications M.A., M.F.A., or Ph.D. in English or M.A. or Ph.D. in closely-related field with a minimum of 18 hours graduate credit hours in English courses. Minimum required level and type of experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities Excellent written and oral communication skills. Experience with Microsoft Office. Preparation and/or experience teaching introductory-level courses in literature and/or composition at the college level. Preferred Qualifications Availability to teach in-person on Old Dominion University’s Norfolk, VA, campus between the hours of 8:00 AM and 3:00 PM, AND one or more of the following: For Literature: ability to teach across genre and period specialties and to include a diverse selection of texts and voices. For Composition: expertise and experience in writing studies pedagogies such as WAC / WID , multi-modality, anti-racism, and/or universal design for learning. Conditions of Employment Location Norfolk, VA Job Open Date 07/24/2024 Application Review Date Open Until Filled Yes Application Instructions Interested candidates must apply via https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/21039 and submit a cover letter outlining preparation and experience for teaching General Education Composition and/or Literature courses; a curriculum vitae; unofficial graduate transcripts; and contact information for 3 professional references. Applications will begin July 22, 2025, and and will recur whenever openings arise. Only those selected for interviews will be contacted. Questions or requests for additional information can be sent to Dr. Mary Beth Pennington, chair of the search committee, via e-mail at mpenning@odu.edu . Telework Friendly No Reasonable Accommodation Request If you are an individual with a disability and require reasonable accommodation, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757)683-3141. Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or © consistent with contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. About the College www.odu.edu/al About the Department http://www.odu.edu/englishdept Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education (website or print) Higheredjobs.com DiverseJobs.com InsightIntoDiversity.com Jobs.Virginia.gov Old Dominion University website Virginia Pilot (website or print) Richmond Times Dispatch (website or print) Academic Keys Other If you selected \"Other,\" how did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for Professional References Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Optional Documents If you have questions: Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty applicants, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757) 683-3042 or Jobsearch@odu.edu . Teaching and Research Faculty applicants, please contact the Office of Academic Affairs at aafacultyemployment@odu.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27467": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor of AI Security (Tenure Track/Tenured,F0144A)",
      "description": "ODU - Job Site | Associate or Full Professor of AI Security (Tenure Track/Tenured,F0144A) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Interest Cards/Categories Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ Applicant Alternative Hiring FAQ Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty Applicants: Contact Human Resources at: (757) 683-3042 HRRecruitment@odu.edu Teaching and Research Faculty Applicants: Contact Academic Affairs at: aafacultyemployment@odu.edu Associate or Full Professor of AI Security (Tenure Track/Tenured,F0144A) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates must complete the online application at https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27439 and include the following: A cover letter describing your relevant qualifications and indicating the rank you would like to be considered for. A curriculum vitae. A statement of research interests. A statement of teaching philosophy. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Contact information for 3-5 professional references. Applications should be submitted by December 15, 2026 for full consideration. The position will remain open until it is filled. Questions about the position should be directed to Daniel Takabi, takabi@odu.edu, Chair of the Trustworthy AI Cluster Hire Initiative. Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Associate or Full Professor of AI Security (Tenure Track/Tenured,F0144A) Department AI CLUSTER HIRE INITIATIVE Position Number F0144A Job Description The School of Cybersecurity at Old Dominion University ( ODU ) invites applicants for an Associate/ Full Professor of AI Security to begin in Fall 2027. This is a Tenure Track/Tenured appointment as part of a cluster hire in Trustworthy AI. We seek exceptional candidates whose research will complement ODU’s areas of strategic emphasis, including fundamental issues related to security, safety, and privacy of AI systems. Successful candidate is expected to develop a vigorous, high impact, externally funded multidisciplinary research program; work closely with other members of the cluster and existing faculty; mentor graduate students; effectively support our teaching mission at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The candidate will be part of the newly established AI Security Institute ( AISI ) , an interdisciplinary university-wide initiative dedicated to advancing the science, technology, and education of AI security and safety. This cluster hire is part of ODU’s Centennial Cluster Initiative which supports the expansion of transdisciplinary research efforts by prioritizing the hiring of multiple faculty positions targeting specific research areas. The Trustworthy AI cluster hire involves interdisciplinary collaboration among School of Cybersecurity, Department of Computer Science, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, and Department of Sociology & Criminal Justice, and builds on existing interdisciplinary strengths at ODU . About ODU : Old Dominion University, located in Norfolk, is Virginia’s forward-focused public doctoral research university with more than 24,000 students, a top R1 research ranking, rigorous academics, an energetic residential community and initiatives that contribute $2.6 billion annually to Virginia’s economy. Old Dominion University was founded in 1930. In preparation for our centennial anniversary, the institution initiated the Centennial Cluster Initiative, a hiring program designed to hire interdisciplinary clusters of faculty around emerging themes. As the first step of that initiative, we seek to hire 25 scholars who can contribute to the university’s growing research and teaching portfolio in the area of artificial intelligence. Those scholars will be housed in departments across campus and work together on scholarly activities related to artificial intelligence. Position Type FullTime Type of Recruitment General Public Type of Recruitment General Public Minimum required education and/or special licenses, registrations, trainings, or certifications A Ph.D. in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or any field closely related to Cybersecurity is required. Minimum required level and type of experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities Ability to teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels Ability to work in multidisciplinary settings A strong research record in AI security demonstrated by peer-reviewed publications, a sustained stream of externally funded multidisciplinary research program Ability to transfer existing funded projects, when feasible, upon appointment and be prepared to pursue new externally funded research opportunities immediately Preferred Qualifications Substantial expertise, experience with recognized scholarship and research in AI security Ability to provide a clear vision and plan for establishing and sustaining a successful externally funded research program through interdisciplinary collaboration with other members of the cluster, faculty in the School of Cybersecurity, Interdisciplinary Schools, and across ODU Ability to mentor junior faculty Conditions of Employment Location Norfolk, VA Job Open Date 11/01/2026 Application Review Date 12/15/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Application Instructions Interested candidates must complete the online application at https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27439 and include the following: A cover letter describing your relevant qualifications and indicating the rank you would like to be considered for. A curriculum vitae. A statement of research interests. A statement of teaching philosophy. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Contact information for 3-5 professional references. Applications should be submitted by December 15, 2026 for full consideration. The position will remain open until it is filled. Questions about the position should be directed to Daniel Takabi, takabi@odu.edu, Chair of the Trustworthy AI Cluster Hire Initiative. Telework Friendly No Reasonable Accommodation Request If you are an individual with a disability and require reasonable accommodation, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757)683-3141. Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or © consistent with contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. About the College About the Department The School of Cybersecurity at ODU was established in 2020 and houses one of the largest cybersecurity programs in the nation with a total of about 1700 students. It represents an interdisciplinary effort bringing together over 40 faculty members with a wide range of expertise in computer science, electrical and computer engineering, information technology, criminal justice, cyber laws, psychology, and philosophy. The school offers a BS in Cybersecurity with majors in cybersecurity, cyber operations, cyber risk management, AI for cybersecurity, MS in Cybersecurity with 4 concentrations including AI Security, AI for Cybersecurity, risk management and Cyber Crime, and newly launched PhD in Cybersecurity. Cybersecurity research is flourishing in the school. Diversity of research projects have been developed by and housed in the school with a total of over $15 million in active research funding from highly competitive programs at the National Science Foundation ( NSF ), Office of Naval Research ( ONR ), National Security Agency ( NSA ), National Institute of Standards and Technology ( NIST ), the Commonwealth of Virginia, and industry. ODU has been designated by NSA as a National Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Research ( CAE -R), a National Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Operations ( CAE -CO), and a National Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense ( CAE -CD). ODU is among a handful of elite universities that have received all three CAE designations. ODU is also home to the Coastal Virginia Center for Cybersecurity Innovation ( COVA CCI ), an engine for research, innovation, and commercialization of next-generation cybersecurity technologies, which is part of the Commonwealth Cyber Initiative and funded by the Commonwealth of Virginia. It is also home to the AI Security Institute and the newly established ODU National Security Institute ( ODU - NSI ) which serves as the central connector of university-wide expertise for advancing national security innovation through research, partnerships and workforce development. For more information, visit: https://www.odu.edu/cyber . Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education (website or print) Higheredjobs.com DiverseJobs.com InsightIntoDiversity.com Jobs.Virginia.gov Old Dominion University website Virginia Pilot (website or print) Richmond Times Dispatch (website or print) Academic Keys Other If you selected \"Other,\" how did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Contact Information for Professional References Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents If you have questions: Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty applicants, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757) 683-3042 or Jobsearch@odu.edu . Teaching and Research Faculty applicants, please contact the Office of Academic Affairs at aafacultyemployment@odu.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27460": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Doctor of Physical Therapy (Non-Tenure Track, F0235A)",
      "description": "ODU - Job Site | Clinical Assistant Professor, Doctor of Physical Therapy (Non-Tenure Track, F0235A) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Interest Cards/Categories Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ Applicant Alternative Hiring FAQ Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty Applicants: Contact Human Resources at: (757) 683-3042 HRRecruitment@odu.edu Teaching and Research Faculty Applicants: Contact Academic Affairs at: aafacultyemployment@odu.edu Clinical Assistant Professor, Doctor of Physical Therapy (Non-Tenure Track, F0235A) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates must apply at https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27423 and attach the following to their online application: A letter of application addressing interest in and qualifications. A current curriculum vitae. A statement of scholarly interests and accomplishments, teaching philosophy, and approaches. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Names, email addresses, and telephone numbers of three academic and professional references. Submit applications by December 4th for full consideration. The position will remain open until it is filled. Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Clinical Assistant Professor, Doctor of Physical Therapy (Non-Tenure Track, F0235A) Department SCHOOL OF PHYSICAL THERAPY & ATHLETIC TRAINING Position Number F0235A Job Description Old Dominion University ( ODU ) invites nominations and applications for a full-time, ten-month Clinical Assistant Professor position focused on Neuroscience in the Doctor of Physical Therapy Program, School of Rehabilitation Sciences, Ellmer College of Health Sciences (https://www.odu.edu/rehabsci), with an appointment effective July 25, 2027. The appointment would be at the level of Clinical Assistant Professor. The Doctor of Physical Therapy Program is situated in the School of Rehabilitation Sciences, Ellmer College of Health Sciences, and graduates approximately 48 students per year. The program employs 11 full-time core faculty and is additionally supported by faculty from within the School of Rehabilitation Sciences. The School also oversees the Faschini Wallach Center for Restorative Therapies, an 11,000 sq ft clinic which provides personalized physical, occupational, and speech therapy for adults and children recovering from injury or illness or living with complex medical conditions. This position includes teaching neuroscience, associated neurologic clinical skills, and courses within the DPT curriculum that align with expertise and experience. Other responsibilities include advising and mentoring students, engaging in Program, School, College, and University service, professional development, and scholarship as required by accreditation standards. Position Type FullTime Type of Recruitment General Public Type of Recruitment General Public Minimum required education and/or special licenses, registrations, trainings, or certifications Earned PhD, DPT , or other relevant doctoral degree from an accredited institution. Demonstrated excellence in teaching. Effective communication skills. Demonstrated ability to collaborate with colleagues. Licensed or eligible for licensure as a physical therapist in Virginia. Candidates must be a graduate of a Commission on Accreditation in Physical Therapy Education ( CAPTE ) accredited physical therapy program or equivalent. Minimum required level and type of experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities Preferred Qualifications APTA membership. Experience teaching entry-level clinical skills and problem-solving in neuroscience curricula Board Certified in Neurological Physical Therapy ( NCS ). Conditions of Employment Location Norfolk, VA Job Open Date 10/28/2026 Application Review Date 12/04/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Application Instructions Interested candidates must apply at https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27423 and attach the following to their online application: A letter of application addressing interest in and qualifications. A current curriculum vitae. A statement of scholarly interests and accomplishments, teaching philosophy, and approaches. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Names, email addresses, and telephone numbers of three academic and professional references. Submit applications by December 4th for full consideration. The position will remain open until it is filled. Telework Friendly No Reasonable Accommodation Request If you are an individual with a disability and require reasonable accommodation, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757)683-3141. Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or © consistent with contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. About the College The Ellmer College of Health Sciences is committed to excellence and innovation in education, research, and service. The college prepares outstanding health professionals for workforce needs in the region and conducts research for the advancement of health and wellness at this critical time in the Commonwealth of Virginia, the nation, and the world. The college has established national and international prominence in our core disciplines through research and the preparation of outstanding health and public health professionals who are leaders in their disciplines and communities. Old Dominion University is a residential, research-intensive public institution with a total student enrollment of about 25,000 students, approximately 6,000 of whom are graduate students. Old Dominion University is a minority-serving institution ( MIS ); one-third of students are from minority backgrounds, and over 1,100 are international students from 94 countries. Old Dominion University has a diverse faculty of over 750, 40% of whom are women. The University’s primary campus is in Norfolk, VA, one of the seven cities that make up the historic Hampton Roads region of Virginia, a major recreation area with a diverse population of 1.7 million and home to the Port of Virginia and the largest naval base in the world. About the Department The School of Rehabilitation Sciences within ODU’s Ellmer College of Health Sciences is a dynamic academic community committed to educating future leaders in health and rehabilitation. Offering comprehensive degree options—including Recreational Therapy (B.S.H.S.), Pre-Clinical Studies, a Master of Science in Athletic Training ( MSAT ), professional doctorates ( DPT , OTD ), and a Ph.D. in Kinesiology & Rehabilitation—the School pairs innovative interprofessional education with active research and clinical centers like the Faschini Wallach Center for Restorative Therapies. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education (website or print) Higheredjobs.com DiverseJobs.com InsightIntoDiversity.com Jobs.Virginia.gov Old Dominion University website Virginia Pilot (website or print) Richmond Times Dispatch (website or print) Academic Keys Other If you selected \"Other,\" how did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently employed by, or have previously been employed by, Old Dominion University or Eastern Virginia Medical Center? Yes No If yes, provide dates of employment. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Statement of Research Interests Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Contact Information for Professional References Optional Documents If you have questions: Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty applicants, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757) 683-3042 or Jobsearch@odu.edu . Teaching and Research Faculty applicants, please contact the Office of Academic Affairs at aafacultyemployment@odu.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27471": {
      "title": "Workforce and Organizational Development Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor (Non-Tenured,F0586A)",
      "description": "ODU - Job Site | Workforce and Organizational Development Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor (Non-Tenured,F0586A) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Interest Cards/Categories Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ Applicant Alternative Hiring FAQ Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty Applicants: Contact Human Resources at: (757) 683-3042 HRRecruitment@odu.edu Teaching and Research Faculty Applicants: Contact Academic Affairs at: aafacultyemployment@odu.edu Workforce and Organizational Development Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor (Non-Tenured,F0586A) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates must apply via https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27399 and attach the following: A cover letter detailing relevant experience with the required and preferred qualifications outlined in this job posting. A curriculum vitae. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Contact information for three professional references. When your application is submitted, the application site will request letters of recommendation from these individuals. Review of applications will begin February 15, 2027, and continue until the position is filled. For questions and inquiries, please contact Dr. Michelle Bartlett, Search Committee Chair, at mbartlet@odu.edu. Posting Details Posting Details Job Title Workforce and Organizational Development Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor (Non-Tenured,F0586A) Department ED FOUNDATIONS & LEADERSHIP Position Number F0586A Job Description Old Dominion University’s Department of Educational Leadership & Workforce Development seeks applications for a full-time Assistant/Associate Professor (10-month appointment with summer employment) in the Workforce & Organizational Development (graduate) program beginning July 2027. Candidates with expertise in human resource development and training, workforce development, and career and technical education are encouraged to apply. The salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. A Ph.D. or Ed.D. is required in a field related to human resource development-training, workforce and organizational development, career and technical education, or equivalent that will enable the candidate to teach graduate courses, advise MS students, and serve on dissertation committees. Responsibilities include: Teaching and developing graduate level online courses, Advising and directing graduate student coursework, Mentoring graduate student research, and Support administrative functions of the MS Workforce and Talent Development program. Previous college teaching and/or business and industry experience in the following fields is preferred: career and technical education, business and industry training/adult education; organizational and workforce development; organizational performance improvement; program evaluation and assessment; project management; consulting; and learning analytics. Position Type FullTime Type of Recruitment General Public Type of Recruitment General Public Minimum required education and/or special licenses, registrations, trainings, or certifications A Ph.D. or Ed.D. is required in a field related to Human Resource Development-Training, Career and Technical Education, Workforce & Organizational Development, or an equivalent that will enable the candidate to specialize in an area of research, teaching, and service. Minimum required level and type of experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities Proven ability to teach online courses effectively. Experience mentoring graduate students. Demonstrated ability to lead academic programs. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively in a diverse academic community. Preferred Qualifications Experience in delivering online courses in different modalities is preferred, e.g., synchronous, asynchronous, and blended. The candidate is expected to demonstrate a commitment to diversity and inclusiveness and a willingness to work in a multicultural setting, as well as a commitment to participating in program governance and decision-making. Experience with program development or curriculum design. Scholarly writing experience, including publishing peer reviewed manuscripts. A background overlapping more than one of career and technical education, human resources training, workforce development, and the community college system. Conditions of Employment Location Norfolk, VA Job Open Date 11/02/2026 Application Review Date 02/15/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Application Instructions Interested candidates must apply via https://jobs.odu.edu/postings/27399 and attach the following: A cover letter detailing relevant experience with the required and preferred qualifications outlined in this job posting. A curriculum vitae. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Contact information for three professional references. When your application is submitted, the application site will request letters of recommendation from these individuals. Review of applications will begin February 15, 2027, and continue until the position is filled. For questions and inquiries, please contact Dr. Michelle Bartlett, Search Committee Chair, at mbartlet@odu.edu. Telework Friendly Yes Reasonable Accommodation Request If you are an individual with a disability and require reasonable accommodation, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757)683-3141. Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Provision The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or © consistent with contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. About the College https://www.odu.edu/education About the Department The Department of Educational Leadership & Workforce Development is one of five departments in the Darden College of Education and Professional Studies. The department has twenty full-time faculty that offer graduate programs in Workforce and Organizational Development, Community College Leadership, Educational Leadership, and Higher Education Leadership. The department offers an undergraduate degree in Occupational & Technical Studies with majors in Fashion Merchandising, Industrial Technology, Training Specialist, as well as a degree in Career & Technical Education with majors in Marketing Education and Technology Education. For more information, visit: https://www.odu.edu/educational-foundations-leadership Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education (website or print) Higheredjobs.com DiverseJobs.com InsightIntoDiversity.com Jobs.Virginia.gov Old Dominion University website Virginia Pilot (website or print) Richmond Times Dispatch (website or print) Academic Keys Other If you selected \"Other,\" how did you hear about this employment opportunity? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Contact Information for Professional References Optional Documents If you have questions: Staff and Administrative & Professional Faculty applicants, please contact the Division of Talent Management and Culture at (757) 683-3042 or Jobsearch@odu.edu . Teaching and Research Faculty applicants, please contact the Office of Academic Affairs at aafacultyemployment@odu.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
